# The book's menu sample with its `none` arm deleted: a lookup can miss, the
# miss is a none, and `describe` has no arm that names one. The check refuses
# the call where the none is provable, which is the language as designed
# (Clay, 2026-09-09: exhaustiveness on arm match "has always been the way the
# language works"); until then the program ran and printed `<none> yen`.
fn describe price
  "{price} yen"

fn quote menu
  describe menu["pocky"]

pub play = print (quote { "dango":350 "taiyaki":500 })
